Lead-DBS
================================================================================

Wyss DBS Localizer is a new implementation of the processing pipeline of Lead-DBS
(https://www.lead-dbs.org, https://github.com/netstim/leaddbs; Copyright (c) 2014-present
the Lead-DBS developers; GNU General Public License, version 3). Its behaviour, defaults
and file formats are modelled on Lead-DBS. The specifications in ``specs/`` were written
from a study of Lead-DBS, its source code and its behaviour; the code outside
``fastwarp/`` was written from those specifications, not by copying Lead-DBS code.
Where a part of Wyss DBS Localizer is nonetheless derived from Lead-DBS, the Lead-DBS
developers keep their copyright in it, it was modified for Wyss DBS Localizer from April
2026 on, and it is distributed under the GNU GPL version 3 like Lead-DBS. Atlas data
copied from Lead-DBS is listed under "Lead-DBS atlas folders" below.

PaCER (AGPL-3.0-only)
================================================================================

The PaCER electrode reconstruction in ``crates/dbsloc-pacer`` is an independent
implementation written from the specification ``specs/10_pacer.md`` and from the paper

  Husch A, Petersen MV, Gemmar P, Goncalves J, Hertel F (2017). PaCER - A fully automated
  method for electrode trajectory and contact reconstruction in deep brain stimulation.
  NeuroImage: Clinical 17, 80-89.

It is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 only
(``AGPL-3.0-only``; full text ``LICENSES/AGPL-3.0-only.txt``), to match the licence of the
original PaCER implementation. Everything else in this repository keeps its own licence.

PaCER is an optional component behind the cargo feature ``pacer``, which is on by default,
so the default builds and the release packages of ``dbs-localizer`` and ``dbsloc``
contain it. Those builds are distributed as a combination of GPL-3.0-only and
AGPL-3.0-only code (GNU GPL version 3, section 13); the network-use condition of the AGPL
(section 13 of the AGPL) therefore applies to the combined program. A build without the
feature (``--no-default-features``, ``docs/LICENSING.md``) contains no AGPL code and is
GPL-3.0-only.

