Atlas data (DISTAL, Allen, etc.)
---------------------------------
Atlas data shipped with Wyss DBS Localizer installers or committed to this repo is listed below with the terms it is shipped under; an atlas is added only by an owner decision recorded in ``docs/ATLAS_DISTAL.md`` (policy and DISTAL citation). Other Lead-DBS atlases are read from the user's Lead-DBS directory or downloaded by the user from the Lead-DBS host (``specs/11_atlases.md`` §10), never shipped.

Lead-DBS atlas folders (``resources/atlases/leaddbs/``)
-------------------------------------------------------
Decision of 2026-10-22 (product owner): the atlas folders under
``resources/atlases/leaddbs/<name>/`` are verbatim copies of the atlas DATA
folders distributed with Lead-DBS (``templates/space/MNI152NLin2009bAsym/atlases/``
of the Lead-DBS data package ``leaddbs_data.zip``, installed beside Lead-DBS git
``5b1008d``, 2026-03-02; the git repository itself ignores ``atlases/``): per-structure NIfTI masks, ``atlas_index.mat``
(names, colours, presets, citation) and ``gm_mask.nii.gz``. No Lead-DBS code is
included. SPDX: ``GPL-3.0-only AND LicenseRef-LeadDBS-Atlas-Terms`` (``REUSE.toml``); the
data is read at run time and is not compiled into any program. Lead-DBS's ``LICENSE.md`` (GNU GPL v3; copied beside the folders as
``resources/atlases/leaddbs/LICENSE.md``) states that the standard-space atlases "included
in the repository" are released under that licence at their owners' request and should not
be used for commercial purposes; commercial users should contact the primary coordinator of
the atlas. The data package holds no licence file, and the Lead-DBS maintainers stated on
2026-11-11 that the atlas packages carry no licence. Owner decision of 2026-11-11: the bundled
folders keep the GPL label and the non-commercial request as Lead-DBS's ``LICENSE.md`` states
them. The software itself is GPL-3.0-only since 2026-11-10, so the GPL label of the data fits;
the owners' request not to use the atlases commercially stays as stated, and the bundled
atlas folders are to be treated as research-only data.

  DISTAL Minimal (Ewert 2017)
    Citation: Ewert S, Plettig P, Li N, Chakravarty MM, Collins DL, Herrington TM,
      et al. (2017). Toward defining deep brain stimulation targets in MNI space:
      A subcortical atlas based on multimodal MRI, histology and structural
      connectivity. NeuroImage. Also: Chakravarty MM, Bertrand G, Hodge CP,
      Sadikot AF, Collins DL (2006). The creation of a brain atlas for image guided
      neurosurgery using serial histological data. NeuroImage 30(2):359-376.

Any other Lead-DBS atlas folder can be used without copying it: point the
3D viewer at a Lead-DBS ``atlases`` directory (``DBSLOC_LEADDBS_ATLASES_DIR`` or
the GUI setting), see ``specs/11_atlases.md`` and ``docs/ATLAS_DISTAL.md``.

