Normative connectome terms (``resources/licenses/connectomes/``)
-----------------------------------------------------------------
The connectome catalogue shows the data owners' terms verbatim before a download and
records their SHA-256 with the acceptance. The texts are compiled into ``dbsloc-pipeline``
and kept as plain files: ``elias2024-dtor985.txt`` (WU-Minn HCP Open Access Data Use Terms of
2013-04-26 and the CC0 1.0 legal code; the three dTOR-985 entries), ``horn2017-mghusc-hcp32.txt``
(MGH-USC HCP Data Use Agreement, 2014), ``ppmi.txt`` (PPMI Data Use Agreement Version 5.0,
April 2026, Publication Policy, funding partners; both PPMI entries), ``cohen2023-gsp1000v2.txt``
(GSP Open Access Data Use Terms 2014-Apr-22 from the Harvard Dataverse record; the copy with
corrected quotation marks is shipped, the byte-exact copy with double-encoded quotes is not),
``loh2020-torpd75.txt`` (CC BY 4.0 of the Zenodo record), ``horn2013-gibbs19.txt``,
``horn2016-nkirs169.txt`` and ``alfatly2023-pediatric100.txt`` (the statements of the Data in Brief
article, INDI / NKI and CoRR; these sources state no licence text, see each file) and
``leaddbs-hosting.txt`` (what lead-dbs.org states about the hosted packages: nothing; plus a
summary of the Lead-DBS maintainers' e-mail of 2026-11-11: the packages carry no licence, and
their use by other software is not explicitly forbidden).
Each file starts with its source URL and the fetch date (2026-10-23) and was copied from the
owner's website, except the e-mail summary in ``leaddbs-hosting.txt`` (no URL, 2026-11-11, our
summary, not a copy); PDF texts were re-flowed (line breaks only). The PPMI agreement may change
"effective immediately upon posting", so these texts are re-checked at every release; a
changed text makes an earlier acceptance count as not accepted. The files are the property
of their owners and are reproduced only to show the terms that apply to the data.

